Q: A number is called happy if:
Replace the number by the sum of the squares of its digits.
Repeat the process.
If you eventually reach 1, the number is happy.
If you start repeating numbers (forming a cycle), it is not happy.

Logic: Store every calculated number in a HashSet.
If we see the same number again → cycle → return false.
If number becomes 1 → return true.

----------------------------------------------
import java.util.HashSet;
class Solution {
    public boolean isHappy(int n) {
        int rem = 0;
        
        HashSet<Integer> hs = new HashSet<Integer>();
        while(n!=1 && !hs.contains(n))
        {
           
            hs.add(n);
            int sum =0;
            while(n>0)
        {
            
            rem = n%10;
            sum = sum +rem*rem;
            n = n/10;
}
        n= sum;
        }
      return n==1;  
    }
}
